h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 574)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed: playback could stop partway through a clip and freeze on a frame</b> while the timecode kept running — most visible on longer clips and in side-by-side compare. The player filled its frame cache and then stopped feeding itself; it now keeps a rolling window ahead of the playhead and recycles what's behind, so a clip plays through to the end however long it is.</li>
<li><b>Fixed: the app could hitch every few seconds while sharing to the web.</b> The share's background housekeeping was rebuilding the whole review four times a second whether or not anything had changed; it now does that work only when a note, a mark, a clip change or a reorder actually happens.</li>
<li><b>Fixed: a web reviewer's play/pause sometimes needed two or three clicks.</b> The host was echoing each transport change back to the sender; it no longer does, and the web player ignores its own echo.</li>
<li><b>No more full-resolution still render while you're playing:</b> a reviewer parking on a frame elsewhere no longer makes the host render a still mid-playback.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
